{"id": "EUVD-2026-76325", "enisaUuid": "80cf6187-d7be-3a91-bcce-c1e5454024de", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxdp: fix zero-copy frame layout\n\nxdp_convert_zc_to_xdp_frame() clones an XSK packet into an order-0 page\nand advertises PAGE_SIZE as its frame size.  It allows the copied frame\nto occupy the page tail needed by skb_shared_info and records zero\nheadroom even when metadata separates the frame header from packet data.\nAn AF_XDP zero-copy packet redirected through cpumap can therefore make\nthe skb overlap skb_shared_info or place it beyond the allocated page.\n\nLimit the copied layout to SKB_WITH_OVERHEAD(PAGE_SIZE) and include the\nmetadata length in frame headroom.  Redirect callers already handle a\nNULL conversion result.\n\nBUG: KASAN: slab-out-of-bounds in skb_gro_receive\nWrite of size 4 at addr ffff88800cf37004 by task cpumap/1/map:1/146\nCall Trace:\n skb_gro_receive (net/core/gro.c:174)\n udp_gro_receive (net/ipv4/udp_offload.c:812)\n inet_gro_receive (net/ipv4/af_inet.c:1539)\n dev_gro_receive (net/core/gro.c:515)\n gro_receive_skb (net/core/gro.c:633)\n cpu_map_kthread_run (kernel/bpf/cpumap.c:395)\n kthread (kernel/kthread.c:436)\n ret_from_fork (arch/x86/kernel/process.c:164)\n ret_from_fork_asm (arch/x86/entry/entry_64.S:255)\nKernel panic - not syncing: KASAN: panic_on_warn set ...", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:42:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:46:26", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dcb6db9ca6515fcd3e00c93ec5e27dc7a0a7012f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/22092730129077c302d8c947bbe0876f0280c528", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ced3e18cd9b9caf630aaa1e1eac305f5192ba896", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6de17275b3ccdf9887568b07e54da2e3597217cf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/444216dacdbebd3e52d5e704facafbb230da09e9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/15d1f3c0dbe7a740f779337deb39f23cd8d002c8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/68d7cc5512238693670fc19c7a615df631e10edf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/71283aaa6c65b3cec84caf1dc78560985737641f"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-81002", "GHSA-w4xj-mpx6-w45f"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.51, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "171493f3-7df2-340e-9094-e531dd48eaa6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b0d1beeff2a97a0cf1965ea8f1d13b8973f22582 <ced3e18cd9b9caf630aaa1e1eac305f5192ba896"}, {"id": "27522fc4-c22d-3f3f-9ae1-876e6e4fc0cd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b0d1beeff2a97a0cf1965ea8f1d13b8973f22582 <444216dacdbebd3e52d5e704facafbb230da09e9"}, {"id": "2c9adec2-b262-3ca6-9c0b-7f85544aa103", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "2e719f4c-b33a-39a0-aa07-8be7400ccbe5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b0d1beeff2a97a0cf1965ea8f1d13b8973f22582 <22092730129077c302d8c947bbe0876f0280c528"}, {"id": "331d474f-e0da-37e8-a7c7-b51974d90bd7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "34147b2a-aec4-3d99-9aeb-3dadf89404ae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "6a2c5aee-1dfd-39ae-89ec-424d8f5de19a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b0d1beeff2a97a0cf1965ea8f1d13b8973f22582 <68d7cc5512238693670fc19c7a615df631e10edf"}, {"id": "70892fea-21be-3aba-a4b6-634b5d40e6db", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b0d1beeff2a97a0cf1965ea8f1d13b8973f22582 <dcb6db9ca6515fcd3e00c93ec5e27dc7a0a7012f"}, {"id": "74a4b789-d053-343e-af5c-89b18cec35b3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "a3d472e2-c83a-3403-bbe9-6818c34346c6", "product": 